The promising tourist I wrote about a couple of weeks ago has turned into my
third ascension!

I've had no joy whatsoever with Tourists before, but this guy had incredible
luck early in the game.  I wrote before about the +4 shield of reflection
dropped by a hill orc in Sokoban, and the gray dragon scales I collected in
the Gnomish Mines.  Those combined with Sting and a pair of gauntlets of
power to make the early game relatively painless.

I got hold of Mjollnir soon after fom saccing, and used it most of the way
to Gehennom - finally enchanted to +6.  Got hold of Magicbane and the PYEC -
which is a fantastic artifact, by the way.  Then I swapped Mjollnir for
two-weaponing with Magicbane and a silver sabre for the rest of the game
(which also meant swapping the GDSM for silver, and ditching the shield of
reflection).  The Magicbane / sabre combination was unstoppable in Gehennom,
when combined with a +4 ring of increase damage.

I geno'ed L, h, ; and disenchanters quite early.  I'm not ready to try
conduct games just yet.  I was quite sparing with wishes, though - just 2
magic markers, a ring of conflict for the Planes, and a helm of opposigte
alignment when the first altar I went to on Astral turned out to be lawful
(the helm made me chaotic, of course, so I ditched it and went looking for
the altar to The Lady).

All in all this felt like a relatively easy game.  No doubt the early lucky
finds helped out a great deal.  But the Planes especially were a walk in the
park.  Conflict sure helped a lot.  And Famine was so much easier to deal
with than Pestilence, who's caused me so many problems in the past.

Tourists are pretty great, I've discovered, if they can survive the early
levels.  They can #twoweapon, advance in every weapon, make good use of
magic, and they get the PYEC, which can make a single instance of a wand
very powerful indeed - and greatly increase the usefulness of certain rings.


